    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "Lost copy: a copy inserted at the end of the loop body overwrites a value still needed after the exit.",
      "narration": "Lost copy: the phi's copy lands at the end of the loop body. When the loop exits, x2 already holds x3, so the later use reads the wrong value.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Lost copy",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "L: x2 = phi(x1, x3)\n   x3 = x2 + 1\n   x2 = x3     ; copy on back edge\n   if c goto L\nuse(x2)  ; wants OLD x2",
          "x": 6,
          "y": 18,
          "w": 88,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "at": 1300
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The copy clobbers x2 on the exit path too.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 48,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "red",
          "at": 2100
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "caption": "Swap: phis are parallel, but sequential copies make the second one read an overwritten value.",
      "narration": "Swap: two phis read each other's old values simultaneously. Emitting them sequentially makes both equal b2, destroying the swap.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Swap problem",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "L: a2 = phi(a1, b2)\n   b2 = phi(b1, a2)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 18,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "at": 1300
        },
        {
          "id": "bad",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "a2 = b2\nb2 = a2   ; reads new a2!",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 36,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "red",
          "at": 2100
        },
        {
          "id": "ok",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "t = a2\na2 = b2\nb2 = t",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 54,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "green",
          "at": 2900
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "The fixes: split critical edges, treat phis as one parallel copy, and break cycles with a temporary.",
      "narration": "Split critical edges so copies get their own block, treat a block's phis as one parallel copy, and break cycles with a temporary.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "The fixes",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Split critical edges: copies get a safe home",
            "Phis of a block = one parallel copy",
            "Sequentialize it; a cycle needs a temp",
            "Or copy phi results into fresh temps first"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 18,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "purple",
          "at": 1300
        }
      ]
