    {
      "duration_ms": 9500,
      "caption": "LLVM's PHIElimination pass lowers phis in machine IR, and the register allocator coalesces most copies away.",
      "narration": "In LLVM, the PHIElimination pass does this on machine IR, splitting critical edges as needed. Register coalescing later removes many inserted copies.",
